Milestone 3 remediation round 1, 2026-09-13: claim sentences rendered from their checks (plans/2026-09-13-evaluation-evidence.md, Milestone 3 with Amendment 4)
Branch evaluation-evidence at 2b9e13f (Amendment 4 on top of 811ca14) with the remediation in the working tree (committed with this section). Same machine and
shell rules as Milestone 3: set -a && source .env && set +a before every command; `env | grep` for RAG_* and the application enable flags: 0 lines. No chat
model, no embedding, no /api/recommendations call, no evaluation snapshot created, no database read by the claims check.

Validation of 811ca14 failed because the checker never compared a claim's text with its check (RAG.md said a sentence could not drift from its check) and
because a metric with more than six decimal places threw an uncaught ArithmeticException (ClaimsCheck.java:391) that ended the whole check. Amendment 4 is the
specification; every bullet is implemented: observed and derived claims carry no text and their sentences are rendered from the check's parameters and the
values found (a fixed template per check type, RAG.md Claims, Sentences), with optional digit-free labels; inferred, unknown, and experiment claims keep free
text, printed with premises, the report's reason, or the experiment and its checked outcome, and screened for causal stems (experiment only) and absolute or
predictive words (always refused); experiment files name the factor, two settings, and two snapshot files, and the check fails unless those snapshots'
recorded properties differ in exactly the factor and the claim's check reads only them or their reports; every path must resolve inside
src/main/java/documentation/live-runs (the evidence root; symbolic links resolved); unknown keys are refused at every level, topK rows included, and a
repeated key is a read error; a ruleRow criterion with absent data fails; any exception in one claim is that claim's problem; the generator reports a file
with unbalanced markers and continues; a block holding a claim without a rendered sentence still compares its other lines; RAG.md Claims rewritten to match
the code (templates, wording stems and limits, experiments, path rule, what the check proves and what people read, dated corrections of the Why, check, and
